  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased capacity of the Government of Portugal to improve the effectiveness of work-life balance and gender equality policies in the world of work at the national level</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Despite progress on advancing key legal and policy provisions to promote gender equality in the labour market in Portugal, gaps in their implementation and monitoring prevail, resulting in persistent gender inequalities and decent work deficits in the world of work. Moreover, as other countries in Europe, Portugal is facing significant demographic changes, with aging populations expected to further increase the demand for care work. ILO in collaboration with the European Commission Reform and Investment Task Force (SG REFORM) is supporting the Government of Portugal to strengthen the institutional capacity to implement, monitor and promote legislative, policy measures and practices to promote gender equality in employment and work life balance. The strategy of intervention entails research and policy support including a comprehensive review of Portugal&#x2019;s gender equality and work-life balance legislation and policies, a comparative analysis of international good practices, and a final assessment with recommendations for strengthening policy and regulatory mechanisms. It also includes capacity-building workshops targeting key stakeholders such as policymakers and social partners.</narrative>
  </description>
